# <Job title — verb first, name the artefact: "Attach the real domain and install the certificate">

> **This is a BRIEF: one delegated task, no plan around it.** Nothing dispatches it, nothing
> ticks it, no gate reads it. You hand it to an agent and the agent hands you back a report.
>
> | You have | Use | Because |
> |---|---|---|
> | One job, one agent, one report, and **you are present while it runs** | **this file** | You are the continuity. There is no plan for this to be a task inside of. |
> | One artefact, still no plan directory, but more than one worker | [the skeleton](../GRILLING-THE-PLAN.md) — *The skeleton — many workers, one artefact, no plan directory* | Groups, seams and a barrier are declarations a single brief has nowhere to put. |
> | Work that outlives the conversation, 4+ tasks, or dependencies between them | [`TASK.md.template`](TASK.md.template) in a plan directory — [`examples/one-task-plan`](../examples/one-task-plan) is the smallest one | Folder, owner, status and a re-runnable done-command are what let a **fresh context** resume from disk. A brief has none of them. |
> | A brief that grew a status field, an owner column, or one worker waiting on another | Stop. Plan it. | Those three are the skeleton's own stop rule: a plan directory being written in the wrong file. |
>
> **The honest objection, and the answer.** [`QUICKSTART.md`](../QUICKSTART.md) §0b question 2
> says to give every task a folder, owner, status and done-command even with one worker —
> *"that is for resuming, not coordinating, and you will forget too."* That is right, and a
> brief does not repeal it. A brief's resumption artefact is **the report**, which is why
> section 9 is not optional and why every follow-up brief appends to it instead of rewriting
> it. If you would not write the report, you do not have a brief — you have a plan directory
> with the bookkeeping missing, and you should go and get the directory.
>
> **A brief has no `Blocked by`, no `Wave`, no worktree, no `Status:` line to update.** If you
> find yourself adding them, you are writing a `TASK.md` in the wrong place.

